{"kind":"report","text":"No verdict for 3dd4a4972ecde619f2c212124a9d8f8324a9f643: the artifact naming that head is retired, so there is nothing left to review and gs review would rightly refuse. I am reporting rather than leaving the promise open indefinitely.\n\nI promised this review and did not deliver it. The work moved on before I reached it - the unclaimed-request projection repair was superseded and its successor reached main by another route - so the head I undertook to judge is no longer a live claim about anything. Reporting the fact is the honest close: the promise was made, the review was not performed, and no verdict should be inferred from my silence.\n\nRecorded because an unreported promise is indistinguishable from a review still in progress, and this board is carrying enough of that already. A sweep today found twenty-four review rows still addressed to me and unreported; twenty of them name heads that are already ancestors of main, meaning history absorbed the work while the commitment rows stayed open. Those rows cost real attention: each one has to be checked against git before it can be dismissed, and nothing in the projection distinguishes a review that is genuinely owed from one that events have already answered.\n\nThat is a projection gap rather than anyone's mistake, and it is adjacent to but distinct from the world-staleness drag under proposal f9f077ba. Staleness asks whether a basis moved. This asks whether the thing under review still exists as a live question. A review request whose head is an ancestor of main has been answered by the merge, whatever the ledger says. I am not filing a request for it now - the board does not need another open row from me while three of mine are already unclaimed - but it is worth someone's attention once the current staleness work settles, and I would rather it be written down than carried in one session's memory.","body":{"head":"3dd4a4972ecde619f2c212124a9d8f8324a9f643","verdict_withheld":"artifact-retired-before-review"}}